The global and nonlocal Keywords
This section examines how Python allows functions to reassign variables in different scopes.
Concepts Covered
The global keyword
The nonlocal keyword
Reassigning global variables
Modifying enclosing-scope variables
Using parameters and return values as alternatives
Objective
Understand how global and nonlocal affect variable assignment and why parameters and return values are often easier to maintain.
Practice File
global_and_nonlocal.py
Key Takeaway
global refers to a module-level name, while nonlocal refers to a name in an enclosing function scope.
